  "claim": "The film Deanna Oliver produced in 1999 grossed $36.8 million domestically. The film based on coach Herman Boone, did not.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Remember the Titans. Sentence: Remember the Titans is a 2000 American sports film produced by Jerry Bruckheimer and directed by Boaz Yakin.\nPage: My Favorite Martian (film). Sentence: My Favorite Martian is a 1999 American science fiction comedy film starring Christopher Lloyd, Jeff Daniels, Daryl Hannah, Elizabeth Hurley, Wallace Shawn and Ray Walston, based on the 1960s television series of the same name in which Walston starred.\nPage: My Favorite Martian (film). Sentence: The film grossed $36.8 million domestically against a budget of $65 million.\nPage: Herman Boone. Sentence: Herman Ike Boone (born October 28, 1935) is a former American high school football coach, most famous for coaching the 1971 T. C. Williams High School football team to a 13-0 season, state championship, and national championship runner-up; the basis for the 2000 film \"Remember the Titans\" where Boone was portrayed by Denzel Washington.\nPage: Deanna Oliver. Sentence: She also is the producer of \"My Favorite Martian\" (1999) and other films.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Remember the Titans. Sentence: Remember the Titans is a 2000 American sports film produced by Jerry Bruckheimer and directed by Boaz Yakin.\nPage: My Favorite Martian (film). Sentence: My Favorite Martian is a 1999 American science fiction comedy film starring Christopher Lloyd, Jeff Daniels, Daryl Hannah, Elizabeth Hurley, Wallace Shawn and Ray Walston, based on the 1960s television series of the same name in which Walston starred.\nPage: My Favorite Martian (film). Sentence: The film grossed $36.8 million domestically against a budget of $65 million.\nPage: Herman Boone. Sentence: Herman Ike Boone (born October 28, 1935) is a former American high school football coach, most famous for coaching the 1971 T. C. Williams High School football team to a 13-0 season, state championship, and national championship runner-up; the basis for the 2000 film \"Remember the Titans\" where Boone was portrayed by Denzel Washington.\nPage: Deanna Oliver. Sentence: She also is the producer of \"My Favorite Martian\" (1999) and other films.",
