        "original_id": "e81a8e43-98c6-5777-a415-26f34e5d082e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Remember the Titans; My Favorite Martian\n- People: Jerry Bruckheimer; Boaz Yakin; Christopher Lloyd; Jeff Daniels; Daryl Hannah; Elizabeth Hurley; Wallace Shawn; Ray Walston; Herman Boone; Denzel Washington; Deanna Oliver\n- Topics: Film production; Box office; High school football; Adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Herman Boone was born on October 28, 1935.\n- Herman Boone is a former American high school football coach.\n- In 1971, Herman Boone coached the T. C. Williams High School football team to a 13-0 season, a state championship, and a national championship runner-up finish.\n- Herman Boone’s coaching of the 1971 T. C. Williams High School football team was the basis for the 2000 film Remember the Titans.\n- In the 2000 film Remember the Titans, Denzel Washington portrayed Herman Boone.\n- My Favorite Martian is a 1999 American science fiction comedy film based on the 1960s television series of the same name.\n- Ray Walston had starred in the 1960s television series My Favorite Martian on which the 1999 film was based.\n- My Favorite Martian stars Christopher Lloyd, Jeff Daniels, Daryl Hannah, Elizabeth Hurley, Wallace Shawn, and Ray Walston.\n- Deanna Oliver was a producer of My Favorite Martian (1999).\n- My Favorite Martian grossed $36.8 million domestically against a $65 million budget.\n- Remember the Titans is a 2000 American sports film.\n- Jerry Bruckheimer produced Remember the Titans.\n- Boaz Yakin directed Remember the Titans.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
